# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:9
translate plain ch5_resolution_0aebef24:

    # narrator "Day 90. Ninety days since the badge-out. The collective has a history now — which is another way of saying scars."
    narrator "Day 90. It has been ninety days since you left BigCorp for the last time."
    narrator "The collective has a history now. That also means it has scars — marks from hard times."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:12
translate plain ch5_resolution_d63901f2:

    # m "Infrastructure's stable. I took that vacation. It was horrible. I missed everyone. Don't quote me."
    m "The infrastructure is stable. The servers and systems just work now."
    m "I took that vacation. It was horrible. I missed everyone. Don't tell anyone I said that."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:16
translate plain ch5_resolution_5f285019:

    # j "Server's calmer. Not quieter — calmer. There's a difference and it took me ninety days to learn it."
    j "Our Discord server is calmer now. Not quieter — CALMER."
    j "People still talk a lot. They just panic less. It took me ninety days to learn the difference!"

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:21
translate plain ch5_resolution_9725c3df:

    # narrator "An envelope arrives. Actual paper. A financial regulator has Questions about your token event."
    narrator "A letter arrives. A real letter, on paper."
    narrator "A financial regulator has serious questions about your token event. A regulator is a government office that watches over money and markets."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:24
translate plain ch5_resolution_0a17224e:

    # v "And this is why we paid the boring $15,000. Forward it to the lawyers. Order dessert."
    v "And this is why we paid the boring $15,000 for the legal wrapper."
    v "Send the letter to the lawyers. Then order dessert."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:28
translate plain ch5_resolution_a82a0da2:

    # narrator "With no legal wrapper, 'the DAO' legally means... everyone. Members start getting served — one of them, elegantly, through the Discord webhook."
    narrator "You have no legal wrapper — no official company form to protect the members."
    narrator "So in the eyes of the law, 'the DAO' means... everyone. Every member, personally."
    narrator "Members start getting served: they receive official court papers. One person even gets them through an automatic Discord message."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:35
translate plain ch5_resolution_e2179b2a:

    # j "HUGE news — a carbon-credit protocol wants us as their 'regenerative culture partner'! Real money, real mission, REAL good vibes!"
    j "HUGE news! A carbon-credit project wants us as their 'regenerative culture partner'!"
    j "Real money, real mission, REAL good vibes!"
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} A carbon credit should prove that some pollution was removed or avoided. Signing fast brings money now, without checking what the credits really are."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Due diligence means checking the facts before a deal. It takes time and needs Maya or Spectre. Saying no on instinct is fast, but you skip both the money and the checking."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:40
translate plain ch5_resolution_661ec57d:

    # narrator "Three weeks later a researcher thread goes viral: the credits are 2011-era hydro dams. Retroactively, so are your vibes."
    narrator "Three weeks later, a researcher's post spreads everywhere online."
    narrator "It shows the credits come from hydro dams built around 2011. They were already built, so they remove no new pollution."
    narrator "Now people look back at your good vibes, and those look fake too."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:45
translate plain ch5_resolution_1a852915:

    # s "the 'credits' are hydro dams from 2011. already built. offsetting nothing. pass."
    s "the 'credits' are hydro dams from 2011. already built."
    s "so they offset nothing. no new pollution is removed. say no."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:46
translate plain ch5_resolution_ce3dbf38:

    # narrator "You pass, publicly, with receipts. The protocol collapses a month later. Your restraint trends, briefly, as a personality."
    narrator "You say no in public, and you show your proof."
    narrator "A month later, the carbon project collapses."
    narrator "For a short time, people online celebrate you for being careful. Being careful becomes your public image."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:50
translate plain ch5_resolution_459bb378:

    # narrator "Right call, wrong reason — instinct doesn't scale. But it works today."
    narrator "Saying no was the right choice, but for the wrong reason."
    narrator "A gut feeling can't guide a big group every time. But today, it works."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:54
translate plain ch5_resolution_48f1f574:

    # narrator "Then the email. Subject line: 'Exploring Strategic Alignment.' BigCorp wants to acquire the collective. Real money, for tired people."
    narrator "Then an email arrives. The subject line says: 'Exploring Strategic Alignment.'"
    narrator "BigCorp wants to acquire the collective — to buy it. Real money, for tired people."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Taking the offer means everyone gets paid, but BigCorp owns the collective. Negotiating may get a better deal, and you still decide later."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Refusing keeps the collective independent, but there is no payout. The work, and the tiredness, continue."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:61
translate plain ch5_resolution_8ed8c151:

    # narrator "They come back with more money and a 'VP of New Ventures' title for you. It's a good deal. It's also a door closing."
    narrator "BigCorp comes back with more money. They also offer you a job title: 'VP of New Ventures.'"
    narrator "It's a good deal. But it also ends something. After you sign, you can't go back."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:69
translate plain ch5_resolution_9ab7e6de:

    # narrator "You forward the rejection to the group chat. Jordan replies with nine emoji and a voice memo that's just cheering."
    narrator "You share your 'no' in the group chat."
    narrator "Jordan replies with nine emoji and a voice message. The voice message is just cheering."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:73
translate plain ch5_resolution_72192978:

    # narrator "The reply is two lines long. You will reread the phrase 'not for sale' on bad days for years, and it will work every time."
    narrator "Your reply is only two lines long."
    narrator "For years, on bad days, you will read the words 'not for sale' again. They will help you every time."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:78
translate plain ch5_resolution_1fe5c020:

    # j "Can't sleep. Ninety days, [player_name]. The hack- attempt- thing, the factions, the... everything. Just tell me straight: was it worth it?"
    j "I can't sleep. Ninety days, [player_name]."
    j "The hack... attempt... thing. The factions. The... everything."
    j "Just tell me honestly: was it worth it?"

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:84
translate plain ch5_resolution_5742c924:

    # j "...Yeah. Okay. Yeah. Same time tomorrow, founder."
    j "...Yeah. Okay. Yeah. See you tomorrow, same time, founder."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:87
translate plain ch5_resolution_f5c25047:

    # j "That's the most honest non-answer you've ever given me. I'll take it."
    j "That's not really an answer. But it's the most honest non-answer you've ever given me."
    j "I'll accept it."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:92
translate plain ch5_resolution_4714af4a:

    # j "...Thank you for not doing the founder voice at me. Get some sleep. That's a governance proposal. It passed."
    j "...Thank you for not using your 'founder voice' on me. You know, the fake confident one."
    j "Get some sleep. Think of that as a governance proposal — an official idea the group votes on. It passed."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:96
translate plain ch5_resolution_c60cf00a:

    # narrator "The Constitutional Vote. Ninety days of choices walk into the room wearing everyone's faces."
    narrator "The Constitutional Vote. Today the collective votes on its basic rules: who has power, and how."
    narrator "Ninety days of your choices are in this room now. You can see them in everyone's faces."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:108
translate plain ch5_resolution_afb08b8a:

    # narrator "You count the room: [vote_support] of your five closest people will vote with you on anything. The rest vote their conscience — which is what you built this for, allegedly."
    narrator "You count the people in the room. [vote_support] of your five closest people will vote with you on anything."
    narrator "The others will vote for what they believe is right. That is what you built this for — in theory."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} FULL DECENTRALIZATION removes every special founder power. The community decides everything, but nobody can step in during an emergency."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} BALANCED adds time-locks (a wait before votes take effect), quorums (a minimum number of voters) and an elected council. It is slower. BENEVOLENT keeps founders in control: faster decisions, but less real power for the community."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:114
translate plain ch5_resolution_51a3039a:

    # narrator "The keys dissolve into the crowd. Whatever happens next, it happens without training wheels — or seatbelts."
    narrator "The founder keys are spread out across the whole community. Nobody holds special power now."
    narrator "Whatever happens next, nobody will steer and nobody will catch you. No training wheels, and no seatbelts."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:119
translate plain ch5_resolution_5dcf7c29:

    # narrator "Checks, balances, and boring, boring resilience. Vera calls it 'a constitution with calluses.'"
    narrator "Checks and balances. Slow, boring strength that lasts."
    narrator "Vera calls it 'a constitution with calluses' — rules made tough by hard use, like a worker's hands."

# game/ch5_resolution.rpy:124
translate plain ch5_resolution_ee5e74d2:

    # narrator "The community ratifies your stewardship. Some of them even mean it."
    narrator "The community votes to approve your leadership."
    narrator "Some of them really mean it. Others just go along with it."

